{"id":"surface:range-habitat-king-eider-2.0.0","speciesId":"species:king-eider","metric":"HABITAT_SUITABILITY_IN_RANGE","unit":"habitat class inside the supported range","sitesSurveyed":122,"sitesDetected":122,"source":{"authority":"North Ground (range and habitat profile)","title":"King eider: habitat opportunity inside its range, methodology 2.0.0","url":"https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?taxon_key=2498350&country=ca&country=us&license=cc0_1_0&license=cc_by_4_0&hascoordinate=true&hasgeospatialissue=false&occurrencestatus=present&year=2000,2026&basisofrecord=human_observation&basisofrecord=preserved_specimen&basisofrecord=material_sample&basisofrecord=machine_observation&basisofrecord=observation&month=9,12&month=1,2","licence":"North Ground surface; inputs under CC BY 4.0 (Copernicus land cover), CC0 1.0 and CC BY 4.0 (occurrence records through GBIF.org)","attribution":"Contains modified Copernicus Global Land Service information (2019). Buchhorn, M. et al., Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe. Range from occurrence records published through GBIF.org (retrieved 2026-09-30) by the 9 datasets credited in content/intelligence/range-habitat/datasets.json.","retrievedAt":"2026-09-30","verifiedAt":"2026-09-30"},"limitations":["How well the land suits king eider, inside the range records place it. Habitat, not a count of animals and not a density.","The range is ground within 30 km of places where openly licensed records confirm the species; where people rarely record wildlife, real range can be missing, and records can be wrong.","Records decide only whether ground is in the range; they never set a cell's colour, so where more people report wildlife does not become where there are more animals. Sea ducks are recorded from shore, piers and ferries; flocks far offshore are under-recorded.","Unshaded ground is outside that range, rated unsuitable inside it, or open water, sea, ice or town the profile does not name as habitat. None of these is a finding that the species is absent.","Land cover is from 2019 and does not know forest age, recent fire or harvest.","Drawn from records made in September to February, so it shows where the species is in the hunting season, not where it breeds.","Hunting geography and seasons play no part in this surface; the zone card says what is legal."],"observationPeriod":{"from":"2000-01-01","through":"2026-09-30"},"methodology":{"id":"methodology:north-ground-range-habitat","version":"2.0.0","effectiveFrom":"2026-09-30","history":[{"version":"1.0.0","detail":"First publication: range from clustered record squares, categorical habitat inside it."},{"version":"2.0.0","detail":"Ground inside the range rated unsuitable kept as its own state; water, sea, ice and town masked for profiles that do not name them; values placed on the grid nodes the renderer samples (1.0.0 sat half a cell south-west); an island rule for sedentary families; elevation and coast requirements; confidence from components rather than record counts alone."}]},"methodologyStatedAs":"Range: ground within 30 km of 0.35° squares holding 2+ openly licensed records since 2000, each within 150 km of another (122 squares, 29406 records, September to February). Habitat: each 0.1° cell's land cover read through this species' categorical profile (core 1, high 0.75, moderate 0.5, low 0.25, unsuitable 0), share-weighted; open water, sea, ice and town the profile does not name are masked. No weight is fitted.","scaleStatedAs":"King eider: habitat opportunity. Colour is the habitat class for this species inside its range — red core, orange and yellow strong, green moderate, blue marginal. Habitat, not a count of animals.","season":{"observedSeason":"September to February records (the hunting season)","matchesHuntingSeason":true,"warning":"Records from September to February only, so this is the species' hunting-season distribution, not its breeding range."},"model":{"id":"model:north-ground-range-habitat-king-eider","version":"2.0.0","claim":"RANGE_HABITAT","inputs":[{"id":"foundation:landcover-cgls-lc100-2019-0.1deg","hash":"sha256:777678b4d6e4bae78f451737b034fda34cd1565f602f15acecc5e8ad1bf7de13"},{"id":"open occurrence records (content/intelligence/range-habitat/inputs/king-eider.records.json)","hash":"sha256:b7eccfedc3b3e040bcda516a11a441554440cdda7fd9fe96973b47a60bc56a43"}],"literature":["Nests on high Arctic tundra, both on the coast and around inland freshwater lakes. Winters on the ocean in the far north, including pack-ice edges; less tied to the coast than the common eider and rare on fresh water such as the Great Lakes. — North Ground's published profile of the species, citing National Audubon Society, King Eider — Guide to North American Birds."],"reading":"In the hunting season: northern ocean within 40 km of land (less tied to the coast than the common eider) is core; fresh water and land are not habitat.","profile":{"family":"SEA_DUCK_SEASON","reachKm":30,"landCover":{"CORE":["SEA"]},"edge":null,"requires":[],"coastKm":40,"season":"HUNTING_SEASON_RECORDS","whyNotRangeHabitat":null},"range":{"confirmedSquares":166,"countedSquares":122,"islandSquares":0,"openRecords":29406,"datasets":9,"months":[[9,12],[1,2]]},"cells":{"painted":4609,"unsuitable":6574,"masked":{"SNOW_ICE":227,"WATER":772,"BUILT":169},"noData":0},"variation":{"classShares":{"LOW":0.067,"HIGH":0.101,"MODERATE":0.095,"CORE":0.737},"usefulVariation":true},"confidenceComponents":[{"component":"range evidence","holds":true,"detail":"29406 records in 122 squares (needs 300 in 30)"},{"component":"habitat concordance","holds":true,"detail":"record squares on moderate-or-better land 40 in 100 against 37 in 100 across the range (ratio 1.08; needs 1)"},{"component":"seasonal applicability","holds":true,"detail":"hunting-season records for the hunting season"},{"component":"source age","holds":true,"detail":"records read 2026-09-30; land cover epoch 2019 (its age is reported with the surface)"},{"